        {
          "id": 3,
          "title": "Implement Storage and Indexing System",
          "description": "Create a system to store generated summaries in both local files and cold storage, with an index to track all summaries",
          "dependencies": [
            2
          ],
          "details": "Implementation details:\n1. Create a new module `summaryStorage.js` for handling storage operations\n2. Implement a function `saveSummaryLocally(date, summary)` that writes summaries to daily_summary.md files in an organized directory structure\n3. Implement a function `uploadToColdStorage(date, summary)` that uses files.upload API to store summaries in cold storage\n4. Create an indexing system that maintains a JSON file tracking all available summaries with metadata\n5. Implement functions to update the index when new summaries are added\n6. Add functions to query the index for retrieving specific summaries\n7. Include error handling for file system operations and API calls\n8. Implement retry logic for failed uploads\n9. Add logging for all storage operations\n10. Write tests for local storage, cold storage (with mocks), and index management\n11. Ensure the system handles edge cases like duplicate uploads and index corruption\n\n<info added on 2025-04-28T09:14:58.903Z>\n## Implementation Details\n\n### Directory Structure\n```\ndata/\n  summaries/\n    YYYY/\n      MM/\n        DD/\n          daily_summary.md\n  index/\n    summaries_index.json\n```\n\n### Index Schema\n```typescript\ninterface SummaryIndexEntry {\n  date: string;           // ISO format date (YYYY-MM-DD)\n  localPath: string;      // Path to local file\n  coldStorageUri?: string; // URI in cold storage (if uploaded)\n  coldStorageName?: string; // Name in cold storage\n  byteSize: number;       // Size of summary\n  createdAt: string;      // ISO timestamp\n  lastUpdatedAt: string;  // ISO timestamp\n  uploadAttempts: number; // Number of upload attempts\n  uploadSuccess: boolean; // Whether upload succeeded\n  checksum: string;       // MD5 hash of content for integrity verification\n}\n```\n\n### Atomic Index Updates\n```typescript\nasync function atomicIndexUpdate(updateFn: (index: SummaryIndexEntry[]) => SummaryIndexEntry[]): Promise<void> {\n  const lockFile = 'data/index/summaries_index.lock';\n  try {\n    // Create lock file\n    await fs.writeFile(lockFile, Date.now().toString());\n    \n    // Read current index\n    const index = await getSummaryIndex();\n    \n    // Apply update\n    const updatedIndex = updateFn(index);\n    \n    // Write to temp file first\n    const tempFile = 'data/index/summaries_index.json.tmp';\n    await fs.writeFile(tempFile, JSON.stringify(updatedIndex, null, 2));\n    \n    // Rename temp file to actual index file (atomic operation)\n    await fs.rename(tempFile, 'data/index/summaries_index.json');\n  } finally {\n    // Remove lock file\n    try { await fs.unlink(lockFile); } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Retry Logic Implementation\n```typescript\nasync function withRetry<T>(\n  operation: () => Promise<T>, \n  maxRetries = 3, \n  delay = 1000\n): Promise<T> {\n  let lastError: Error;\n  \n  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++) {\n    try {\n      return await operation();\n    } catch (error) {\n      lastError = error as Error;\n      console.warn(`Attempt ${attempt} failed: ${error.message}`);\n      \n      if (attempt < maxRetries) {\n        // Exponential backoff with jitter\n        const jitter = Math.random() * 0.3 + 0.85; // 0.85-1.15\n        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay * Math.pow(2, attempt-1) * jitter));\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  \n  throw lastError;\n}\n```\n\n### Integrity Verification\n```typescript\nimport crypto from 'crypto';\n\nfunction calculateChecksum(content: string): string {\n  return crypto.createHash('md5').update(content).digest('hex');\n}\n\nasync function verifySummaryIntegrity(date: string): Promise<boolean> {\n  const index = await getSummaryIndex();\n  const entry = index.find(e => e.date === date);\n  \n  if (!entry) return false;\n  \n  const content = await fs.readFile(entry.localPath, 'utf8');\n  const currentChecksum = calculateChecksum(content);\n  \n  return currentChecksum === entry.checksum;\n}\n```\n</info added on 2025-04-28T09:14:58.903Z>",
